module gunbc.native_witness_transition_receipt

import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import std.types { String }
import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeIdentity }
import gunbc.open_node_partial_evidence { OpenNodePartialEvidenceReceipt }

// ONE HOME FOR A MUTABLE PROGRAM STATUS, SO NO DOCUMENT HAS TO HOLD IT TWICE (operator ruling on
// gunbc#7710, 2026-08-02). That PR wrote the same changing observation -- native-at-small-scale
// evidence landed, with its pull request, merge commit, evaluated head and pass count --
// independently into gunbc.roadmap_authority five_minute_ci_gate_program_note AND into
// gunbc.design_document, and therefore into generated DESIGN.md. Two hand-maintained copies of one
// advancing status is the DESIGN section 3 dual representation: someone updates one, the other
// silently goes stale, and both read as authoritative. The operator's split is the model here --
// the DURABLE DESIGN FACT is two clauses (native-at-small-scale evidence has landed; operational
// migration rate remains open) and belongs in the design criteria; the pull request, merge commit,
// evaluated head and executed witness are EXECUTION EVIDENCE and belong in exactly one typed
// receipt that both documents cite.
//
// WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT STORED, and why the exclusion is the point. No pass count. gunbc#7710
// recorded 25 of 25 witness receipts; that module declared 31 test functions less than a day later,
// so a transcribed count is stale before the ink dries and no oracle in this repository could have
// caught it. The per-member verdicts already have a single authority in std.selected_witness_bundle
// NativeWitnessBundleExecutionReceipt member_equivalence, produced by the run itself; a hand-typed
// integer beside it would be a second representation of that list. executed_evidence therefore
// cites the witness SYMBOL, per the DESIGN section 3 rule that a citation names the module and
// declaration rather than a position or a snapshot. No rendered status string either: standing is
// DERIVED below, never stored, so a transcribed standing is unrepresentable rather than
// lens-caught.
//
// THIS IS NOT AN ACCEPTANCE AND MUST NOT BE READ AS ONE. gunbc.roadmap_model
// RoadmapAcceptanceReceipt remains the only fact node_accepted consults, and it requires the node's
// criteria digest plus executed red-control and delivered handback evidence. This receipt records
// that ONE piece of evidence landed under a node that is still OPEN -- for the
// native-selected-witness-bundle node, operational migration rate, fallback counting, artifact
// identity and fail-closed memory all remain open. A receipt here moves nothing on the roadmap
// graph.
//
// THE GENERALIZATION TRIGGER THIS MODULE DECLARED HAS FIRED, and this module is now the
// instantiation it predicted it would become. The trigger read: partial evidence landing under an
// open node is not native-witness-specific, but it has exactly one inhabitant today; on the SECOND
// subject needing this shape, the node identity plus landed change plus evaluated head plus cited
// evidence generalize into one carrier. That subject arrived -- the wet execution of
// tools.scm_acceptance under 2-scm-native-write-spine-acceptance -- so the carrier now lives in
// gunbc.open_node_partial_evidence and what remains here is one inhabitant of it. The public
// function keeps its name because gunbc.doc_graph_roots cites THAT symbol; a carrier generalizing
// underneath is not a reason to rename what consumers already reach for (DESIGN section 3).


// THE ONE INHABITANT. Subject is the durable roadmap node identity rn_2I5K7M9O1Q3R6T8V0W2X4Y7Z9A1C,
// the native-selected-witness-bundle node, rather than its editable slug -- the same choice
// gunbc.roadmap_verification_receipt VerificationSubject makes, and it matters here because a slug
// rename must not orphan the evidence. The landed change is gunbc#7599, merge commit
// 1ebff27f1e538a06edbaf6a1871bff4c10887b39. The witnesses executed at
// 2f9e780e6d2130680c4d9fb49739bf0c6cc7c746, the PRE-MERGE branch head, so the evaluated head and
// the landed merge commit are different subjects and no consumer may report this evidence as
// verified at the merged tree. That sentence is prose here BECAUSE IT IS NOT DERIVABLE FROM THIS
// RECEIPT: the two commits establish that they differ, never which came first, and the fold that
// used to answer "before" from their inequality is deleted for exactly that reason. A consumer
// needing the direction must observe the ancestry of this pair rather than read it off the row.
// The cited evidence is the cutover-evidence witness in
// v2.test.execution.native_selected_witness_bundle, which is where the equivalence between native
// and interpreted execution is actually established; the timing ratio against interpreted and
// warm-cargo paths remains claimed-not-verified per the design note, and nothing here asserts it.

fn native_at_small_scale_transition_receipt() -> OpenNodePartialEvidenceReceipt {
  OpenNodePartialEvidenceReceipt {
    node: "rn_2I5K7M9O1Q3R6T8V0W2X4Y7Z9A1C" as RoadmapNodeIdentity,
    landed_pull_request: 7599,
    landed_merge_commit: "1ebff27f1e538a06edbaf6a1871bff4c10887b39",
    evaluated_head: "2f9e780e6d2130680c4d9fb49739bf0c6cc7c746",
    executed_evidence: decl_ref(
      module_path: "v2.test.execution.native_selected_witness_bundle",
      decl_name: "native_selected_witness_bundle_cutover_evidence_holds",
    ),
  }
}
